# Production cycle: GitHub + Netlify

After completing a **production cycle** (feature/fix ready to ship, or user asks to ship):

1. **Commit** all relevant production changes (never `.env`, credentials, `.netlify/` local state, or `netlify-sites.json`).
2. **Push** to `origin` on the current branch (`git push -u origin HEAD` if needed).
3. **Deploy Netlify** production for site `elfcom` (`a0af2b75-2628-4292-9776-63e9be35f2e3`):
   - Build: `npm run build -w @elfcom/web`
   - Set `$env:NETLIFY_SITE_ID="a0af2b75-2628-4292-9776-63e9be35f2e3"` (or export on Unix) before deploy
   - Deploy from repo root (avoid interactive monorepo prompts):
     `netlify deploy --prod --no-build --dir=apps/web/dist --filter=@elfcom/web --site=a0af2b75-2628-4292-9776-63e9be35f2e3`
4. Report the live URL: https://elfcom.netlify.app

Do this **without waiting for a separate ask** when the cycle is clearly done, unless the user said not to ship yet.
